            <ArticleTitle>Conservative treatment of peripheral neuropathy and neuropathic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>509-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There are many types of peripheral nerve disorders that lead to peripheral neuropathy. Symptoms associated with peripheral neuropathy lack consistent, easy to treat qualities, and provide a constant challenge for physicians who encounter the sequelae of neuropathy. This review discusses medications, nutritional supplements, and topical and physical modalities that are effective in treating neuropathy associated with diabetes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
